SUMMARY:Freethought Walking Salon: How Do We Build Community Without Churc
 h?
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\nChurches have long provided mor
 e than religion: friendship\, practical help\, ritual\, belonging\, and pe
 ople who show up when life gets hard.\nWhat could a freethought community 
 provide instead?\n\n### Route\n\n* **Meet:** north-east side of Penn Squar
 e\, on E. King St.\n* **Blazin’ J’s\, 15 E King St** — savory bite\n
 * **Aura Little Cafe\, 44 N Queen St** — coffee\, tea\, or light snack\n
 * **Ewell Plaza/Binns Park\, 123 N Queen St** — main seated discussion s
 top\n* **Lancaster Sweet Shoppe\, 141 N Duke St** — dessert finish\n\nTo
 tal walking is roughly **0.7 mile**.\n\n### Questions\n\n* What do people 
 actually get from church communities besides religion?\n* What kind of sup
 port should LFS provide when someone is sick\, lonely\, grieving\, moving\
 , or simply needs company?\n* What recurring rituals or gatherings could c
 reate belonging without becoming church-like?\n* **Closing:** What would m
 ake LFS feel like your community\, not just a Meetup group?\n\nFood and dr
 inks are purchased individually.\n\n**Parking:** Penn Square Garage\, 28 S
  Duke St\, approximately a 2–3 minute walk from our meeting point.\n**We
 ather:** postponed if rain or unpleasant walking conditions are expected.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 316401734/
